{"Bash":"gh issue create \
  --repo SaverinOnRails/yin \
  --title "Bug: transitions on static images spin to completion in one frame (no animation)" \
  --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Description

When applying a wallpaper transition to a static image (JPEG, PNG, etc.), the transition completes instantly with no visible animation. On multi-monitor setups the symptom is more visible: monitors update one-by-one rather than simultaneously.

## Root cause

In `Monitor::resumeTransition()`, the final `render()` call — which is intended to refresh the \"from\" texture once after a transition completes — is placed **outside** the `if (progress >= 1.0f)` block:

```cpp
if (progress >= 1.0f) {
    m_transitionState = nullptr;
}
// BUG: runs on every transition frame, not just on completion
if (m_wallpaper->m_isSingleFrame) {
    render();
}
```

Because `m_transitionState` is still set when `progress < 1.0`, the recursive `render()` call re-enters `resumeTransition()` on every frame. This spins the entire transition to completion inside a single `onFrame()` callback without ever returning to the event loop — making it appear as an instant snap.

Static images are affected because `m_isSingleFrame` is only `true` for them; videos call `decodeNextFrame()` instead and take a different path.

## Fix

Move the `render()` call inside the completion block so it only fires once, after the transition ends:

```cpp
if (progress >= 1.0f) {
    m_transitionState = nullptr;
    // Refresh from-texture once so the next transition doesn't start
    // from a stale frame (static images stop rendering after this).
    if (m_wallpaper->m_isSingleFrame) {
        render();
